():\\n    validation_rules = validate_data(data)\\n    regex_pattern = create_regex_pattern(validation_rules)\\n    count = test_regex_against_data(regex_pattern, data)\\n    complexity = 'Low' if count == 0 else 'Medium' if count < len(data['brand']) * 2 else 'High'\\n    reasoning = f'The regex pattern failed to match {count} values.'\\n\\n    output = generate_output(validation_rules, regex_pattern, complexity, reasoning)\\n\\n    print(\\"HERE IS THE FINAL RESULT\\")\\n    print(output)\\n    \\nif __name__ == \\"__main__\\":\\n    main()\\n```\\n\\nThe final result will be:\\n{\\n  'Column Name': 'Brand',\\n  'Column Type': 'object',\\n  'Business Rules': ['Brand must have exactly 8 unique values.'],\\n  'RegEx Pattern': '^[a-zA-Z\\\\s-]+$', \\n  'Complexity': 'Low',\\n  'Reasoning': 'The regex pattern failed to match 0 values.'\\n}", "total_unique": 8}	2026-05-26 05:08:27.339507+00			llama3.2:3b	New Version	\N
