ailed.\\")\\n```\\n\\n**Final Output (template 5):**\\n\\nHERE IS THE FINAL RESULT\\n- Column Name: gender\\n- Column Type: object\\n- Business Rules: a. The column should only contain 'Female' or 'Male'. b. Unrecognized values will be considered invalid. c. Empty strings or whitespace characters are not allowed.\\n- RegEx Pattern: r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\\\.\\\\d+)?$'\\n- Complexity: Low\\n- Reasoning: This pattern is simple and easy to understand, making it suitable for a categorical column like gender. The regex pattern handles both 'Female' and 'Male' with an optional decimal place.", "total_unique": 2}	2026-05-26 06:14:32.580553+00	a. The column should only contain 'Female' or 'Male'. b. Unrecognized values will be considered invalid. c. Empty strings or whitespace characters are not allowed.\n-	^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.\\d+)?$	llama3.2:3b	New Version	\N
